---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/paths';
---
<SiteLayout title="The kits" active="kits/">
<p class="eyebrow">Catalogue / 001</p>
<h1>The kits.</h1>
<p>One system. Framework-specific rules where they matter.</p>
<div class="two">
<article class="kit">
<img src={sitePath("art/kit-react.svg")} alt="React / Node software cover">
<div>
<p class="tag">01 / Stable default</p>
<h2>React / Node</h2>
<p>Agent skills and JS/TS gates, component inventory, hooks and CI template.</p>
<a href={sitePath("manual/")} >Install the default →</a>
</div>
</article>
<article class="kit">
<img src={sitePath("art/kit-author.svg")} alt="Author guide software cover">
<div>
<p class="tag">02 / Author guide</p>
<h2>Build a kit</h2>
<p>Extend the shared system using preset manifests. Experimental presets require real-world validation.</p>
<a href="https://github.com/hyperbolictonic/opencode-anti-slop/tree/master/presets">Read preset documentation ↗</a>
</div>
</article>
</div>
</SiteLayout>
